This chapter shares only Screen, Input, Player, Practice, control, explorer, drill and ready.

Use the page library.

A control has an action (text).
A control is ready when its action is not "".
An explorer has a column (number), a row (number) and a step count (number).
A drill has a field note (text).

There is a canvas called Screen whose width is 160 and whose height is 144.
There is a control called Input whose action is "".
There is an explorer called Player whose column is 72 and whose row is 80 and whose step count is 0.
There is a drill called Practice whose field note is "Waiting for calibration".




